# The compiler's line of the #error starts with the header's path on the machine, so the
# message is a contains: line. wasip2 and wasip3 have the same message in a compile-diagnostic
# (test/messages/sodium_not_linked); compile-diagnostic is clang's and skips Emscripten, so this
# fixture is the Emscripten one.
[all]
targets: emscripten
build: fails
# tag::messages[]
contains: webcpp::crypto: the backend libsodium is used and not linked. In the program's Jamfile, add /third_party//sodium beside /webcpp/crypto//crypto, as in: exe app : app.cpp /webcpp/crypto//crypto /third_party//sodium ; (without b2: define WEBCPP_CRYPTO_HAS_SODIUM=1 and link libsodium built with webcpp's src/canary_sodium.c)
# end::messages[]
